# Qwen3.6-35B-A3B served locally by oMLX on Apple Silicon (the model this
# directory's README walks through downloading).
# oMLX loads a whole model directory and picks per request, so MODEL names what
# opencode asks for — it is not a launch flag.
PROVIDER omlx
# MODEL must match a model your oMLX actually serves — its directory name or an
# alias. If you downloaded something else, change this: list what yours exposes
# with `curl -H "Authorization: Bearer $OPENAI_API_KEY" localhost:8000/v1/models`.
# A name oMLX does not have is rejected with "model not found".
MODEL    Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-4bit
CONTEXT  32768                  # opencode's context window
PRESET   ./preset.ini           # `outfit serve` launches omlx-cli from this
# BASEURL http://127.0.0.1:8000/v1   # uncomment for a non-default host/port
